I would say... 2. Yes, some of the time. It's not all the time, but it's definitely something that happens regularly. It feels really draining and frustrating.

.. all the time, it feels like. I'm constantly worried about the baby's health and safety. I know it's normal to worry, but it's like, I'm on edge all the time. I'll be lying in bed at night, and I'll start thinking about all the terrible things that could happen, and I just can't turn it off. It's like my mind is racing, and I feel so on edge. Even when I know it's irrational, I still can't shake the feeling.

